<title>GERMANY: Alcatel SEL sees sales growth.</title>
<headline>Alcatel SEL sees sales growth.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alcatel SEL, German unit of France's Alcatel Alsthom, expects its 1997 sales to grow over 10 percent in 1997 to over five billion marks, chairman Roland Mecklinger said on Friday.</p>
<p>In the text of a speech prepared for the annual shareholders' meeting, Mecklinger repeated the company's forecast it would return to operating profit this year, after an operating loss of 103.9 million marks last year, and said it should already have posted a profitable first half.</p>
<p>Sales in 1996 were 4.8 billion marks.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
